From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zyang2 <zyang2@zoo-003.maas>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:04:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Raft spec: a follower may refuse any AppendEntries (S1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LRejectAppendEntries loses its guard. Any server, in any state, may
decline an AppendEntries: its state is unchanged and it sends one
AppendResponse{term: its current term, success: false, match_index: 0,
read_ctx: 0}. raft.tla's reasons (stale term, prev-log mismatch, wrong
append position) and A7's entry-less append at prev 0 remain admitted;
so are reasons the abstract state cannot see, such as a stopped or fenced
server, an unrecognised sender or an undecodable payload.

Why this is still Raft: a refusal is observationally a lost message plus
an unsuccessful reply, which the network can already produce, and a
leader can do nothing with an unsuccessful reply but move next_index,
which LHandleAppendReject treats as unconstrained bookkeeping. The same
argument leaves LRejectVote and LStepAside unguarded.

Proof maintenance: one hint in lemma_follower_commit_prefix_advanced_common,
assert(s_ != s) (the commit index moved, so the step is no refusal).
Without it the lemma exceeds its rlimit in the full crate even at 1000;
with it the original rlimit 150 holds. Full crate under Verus
0.2026.08.02.b677dd5: 2129 verified, 0 errors (as before the change).

Plan item: S1 (docs/verus/modification-plan.md §4.2, Mako repo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
