+**S1 (unguarded refusal).** `LRejectAppendEntries` loses its guard (the three raft.tla reasons
+plus A7's prev-0 entry-less case). A refusal changes no state and sends only an unsuccessful
+response at the sender's own term; a leader can do nothing with it but move `next_index`, which
+`LHandleAppendReject` treats as unconstrained bookkeeping. So declining an append is
+observationally a loss plus an unsuccessful reply, which the network can already produce, and the
+same argument that leaves `LRejectVote` unguarded applies. It admits refusals whose reasons the
+abstract state cannot see: a stopped or fenced server, an unrecognised sender, an undecodable
+payload. Proof maintenance: one hint in `lemma_follower_commit_prefix_advanced_common`,
+`assert(s_ != s)` (the commit index moved, so the step is no refusal); without it the lemma
+exceeds its rlimit in the full crate even at 1000, since the old guard no longer prunes the
+reject case.
+
 **Round 1 (filling holes against raft.tla)**: the up-to-date check for RequestVote
 (`candidate_log_ok`), prev-log consistency for AppendEntries (`prev_log_ok` + `append_pos_ok`), and
 AppendEntriesResponse with success=FALSE (new action `LRejectAppendEntries`; the impl used to drop it
